//RS // ── binary.Reader / text.Cursor (D-SHIFT1, c7shift) ──────────────────────────
//RS // The "shift" kernel from linear stream parsing (Jai's `shift` primitive),
//RS // without a dedicated operator (D-SHIFT1=A rejected that). `Reader` owns its
//RS // byte buffer plus a read position; the borrowed constructor copies its input,
//RS // while the lowering-only owned constructor transfers an already-owned buffer.
//RS // Every read is fallible — a bounds miss is an ordinary `Err`, never a panic or
//RS // silent truncation.
//RS //
//RS // I9: this file is the ONE implementation. `Codegen/mod.rs` splices it verbatim
//RS // into the emitted AOT prelude (`include_str!`), and the canonical TIR
//RS // evaluator calls the same functions directly (`eval/handles.rs`), so quick-run
//RS // and full build read the same bytes and produce the same error text.
//RS // It must stay std-only and free of `crate::` paths: the AOT copy compiles at
//RS // the root of a generated program, not inside this crate.
